# The working tree in C:\inetpub\personalroot\IESA *is* the deployment, so an
# unresolved merge is a live site outage: Git's default text merge writes
# <<<<<<< markers into the very files team-scores.ashx reads and the browser
# parses, turning a routine conflict into invalid JSON being served.
#
# These caches are generated by Update-IesaScores.ps1 on a schedule (several
# times a day, on more than one machine), so a line-level merge of two captures
# is never what is wanted - one capture or the other is correct, never a blend.
#
# "-merge" selects the binary merge strategy: on conflict Git keeps the local
# version in the working tree and marks the path conflicted, without inserting
# markers. The site keeps serving valid JSON while the conflict is resolved.
# Resolve by choosing a side deliberately, or simply by re-running the updater:
#
#     git checkout --theirs 2026/scores-7th.json   # take the incoming capture
#     git checkout --ours   2026/scores-7th.json   # keep the local capture
#     .\2026\Update-IesaScores.ps1                 # or regenerate both
#     git add 2026/scores-7th.json
#
# Diffs are deliberately left enabled: the caches are pretty-printed over
# thousands of lines, so a textual diff is still readable and is how a capture
# is checked for unexpected score regressions.
2026/scores-*.json -merge
2026/scores-*.js   -merge

# Same reasoning for the other generated caches the pages load at runtime.
2026/bracket-*.json        -merge
2026/bracket-*.js          -merge
2026/regional-seeds-*.json -merge
2026/regional-seeds-*.js   -merge
